Looking at the code, it appears that monsters decide to
engage you based on range.  At some range they think
they are fighting you and start taking combat actions.
Combat actions include melee, missiles, zapping a list
of wands, casting a list of spells, reading scrolls and
quaffing potions.  They only do what they can in their
current situation.

Here's what I see as a disconnect, and I suspect it is
deliberate - Most of the actions depend on a line of
sight while quaffing does not.  Get within range that
the monster decides it's fighting you and it will go
through the line of sight checks and eventually fall
back to quaffing or reading.  In the big room I suspect
it will happen a bit less often because monsters usually
have a line of sight the entire way.  They will advance
shooting arrows until they run out and such before
quaffing.  Only monsters with no other item will quaff
in that case I suspect.



